	- added youtube performances (the real book refers to Bill Evans - 'From Left To Right').
	TODO:
	- check the chords (real book).
	- check the tune (real book).
	- hear the tune to check that it is right and adjust the tempo.
	- the handwriting of the melody is very crowded and hard to read; every bar needs checking against a recording, especially the ones below.
	- intro: the book prints F#maj7 and G7(#11) followed by two bars each marked with a two bar repeat sign, then F#maj7 and the E7 pickup bar. This is typed as F#maj7, G7(#11), F#maj7, G7(#11), F#maj7, E7.
	- A bar 2 (and the same bar of the last A): the sixteenth note figure is hard to read and does not add up to four beats as printed; the tied C sharp is typed as a half note.
	- B bar 2 (A7sus4) and B bar 3 (Dmaj7): pitches and accidentals are unclear (the accidental before the first note of B bar 3 is typed as a sharp).
	- the double bar at the end of B seems to carry repeat dots, with no start repeat sign; B is not repeated here.
	- C bar 4 (F#7 alt): the rhythm and the low notes are unclear.
	- C bars 12 and 14 (F#7 alt, E7 alt) and the bars around them: the book writes a second, lower voice (long notes and some eighths) under the melody; only the upper voice is typed.
	- C bar 11 (C#7 alt): the book draws a short dash under the staff that is not typed.
	- last A bars 5-6 (F#7, B7): the tied note is drawn between G and A, typed as G.
	REMARKS:
	- the book writes '7 alt.' chords, which are written here as 7#5#9.
	- the book has no section letters; the sections here follow the double bars and repeat signs of the page.
{% endif %}
